# Build output
*.obj
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.exp
*.lib
*.ilk
*.idb

# Runtime data.
#
# wrlines_data\demos\ holds demos fetched from Momentum's leaderboard, which
# carry other players' names and SteamID64s just as the ones the game
# downloads do.
#
# Not just build noise: wrlines_data\paths\ holds .wrpath files derived from
# other players' downloaded demos, and every one of them carries that player's
# name and SteamID64. They are yours to generate locally, not to publish.
# wrlines.log and wrlines_offsets.ini are per-machine too.
#
# wrlines_data\into_game.txt lists the demos copied into the game's own replay
# folder, and it is the ONLY thing the removal button will delete -- so it is
# per-machine state that must not be shared, and losing it strands those copies
# rather than corrupting anything.
#
# wrlines_data\friends.txt is the SteamID64 of every one of YOUR Steam friends,
# written so the fetch script can ask the leaderboard about them. That is other
# people's identities, in a file, for your convenience -- it does not leave your
# machine except as the ids in that one request, and it must not leave this
# repository at all.
wrlines_data/

# Third-party trees, cloned by hand -- see README, "Build".
imgui/
minhook/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Dear ImGui's own settings file. Inert here -- wr_imgui.cpp sets
# io.IniFilename = NULL, so nothing reads or writes it -- but a stray copy turns
# up in the working tree and is not ours to ship.
imgui.ini

# Editors / IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
*.sln
*.vcxproj*
